meta {
  name: 15 - Issues Archival Sweep
  type: graphql
  seq: 15
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}
  body: graphql
  auth: inherit
}

body:graphql {
  query IssuesArchivalSweep {
    archived: issues(
      first: 250
      includeArchived: true
      filter: {archivedAt: {gt: "2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z"}}
    ) {
      nodes { id identifier updatedAt archivedAt }
      pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
    }
    withoutIncludeArchived: issues(
      first: 250
      filter: {archivedAt: {gt: "2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z"}}
    ) {
      nodes { id identifier archivedAt }
      pageInfo { hasNextPage }
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Reference: https://linear.app/developers/filtering

  The second, independent sweep the Issues stream needs in order to observe archival at
  all. Runs on its OWN cursor (`archivedAt`), separate from the `updatedAt` cursor that
  drives `11 - Issues Ascending Sweep`.

  Necessary because archiving does not touch `updatedAt` — see
  `08 - Archival Capability Matrix` for the verified negative and the full reasoning.

  **Limitation / observed finding** (confirmed 2026-08-04, after `Seeding/D2` archived
  EST-2):

  - `archived` -> **1 row**: `EST-2`, `archivedAt: 2026-08-04T18:13:09.393Z`, and
    `updatedAt` still at the original bulk-seed value `2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z`. That
    single row is the whole argument for this request existing: it is invisible to an
    `updatedAt` sweep, and visible here.
  - `withoutIncludeArchived` -> **0 rows**. **`includeArchived: true` remains mandatory**
    even when filtering on `archivedAt` — the filter alone does not opt archived rows back
    into the response. Omitting it yields a silently empty archival pass, which would look
    exactly like "nothing was archived".

  Two design constraints this pass inherits:

  1. **End-of-sweep checkpointing only.** `IssueSortInput` has no `archivedAt` member, so
     this pass cannot sort by its own cursor. Without an ascending sort there is no
     guarantee that rows arrive in `archivedAt` order, so a per-page checkpoint could
     advance past unread rows. Checkpoint once, at `max(archivedAt)` observed, after
     `hasNextPage` goes false.
  2. **`gt` is safe here, unlike the `updatedAt` cursor.** `archivedAt` is set once, at
     archival, and is not subsequently churned by unrelated edits, so the tie-group hazard
     that forces `gte` on `updatedAt` (see `07 - Cursor Filter Boundary`) is far weaker.
     `gte` is still the more conservative choice and costs only a re-emit; the plan uses
     `gte` uniformly for consistency.

  Note the archived document still carries its stale `updatedAt`. Downstream, `archivedAt
  != null` is the tombstone — do not infer archival from `updatedAt` movement.
}


example {
  name: 200 — archivedAt filter finds EST-2; includeArchived still mandatory

  request: {
    url: https://api.linear.app/graphql
    method: POST
    mode: graphql

    body:graphql: {
      query IssuesArchivalSweep {
        archived: issues(
          first: 250
          includeArchived: true
          filter: {archivedAt: {gt: "2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z"}}
        ) {
          nodes { id identifier updatedAt archivedAt }
          pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
        }
        withoutIncludeArchived: issues(
          first: 250
          filter: {archivedAt: {gt: "2026-08-01T00:00:00.000Z"}}
        ) {
          nodes { id identifier archivedAt }
          pageInfo { hasNextPage }
        }
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    headers: {
      x-complexity: 7
      x-ratelimit-requests-limit: 2500
      x-ratelimit-requests-remaining: 2486
      x-ratelimit-complexity-limit: 3000000
      x-ratelimit-complexity-remaining: 2999993
    }

    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }

    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "archived": {
              "count": 1,
              "rows": [
                {
                  "id": "EST-2",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T21:35:03.808Z",
                  "archivedAt": "2026-08-04T18:13:09.393Z"
                }
              ]
            },
            "withoutIncludeArchived": {
              "count": 0,
              "rows": []
            }
          }
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
